This directory is a modified copy of the gpui 0.2.2 crate published by
Zed Industries, Inc. (https://github.com/zed-industries/zed, crates/gpui).
zyuapp changed it in 2026. The changes:

- Page zoom: layout pixels map to zoom-scaled window points; border widths
  snap to whole pixels at the zoom.
- Text: letter spacing; truncation keeps shaped lines; text layouts keep the
  inherited colour and decorations so hover, press and focus styles recolour
  them at paint; dotted and dashed underlines with a set offset.
- Layout: boxes snap to whole pixels from the root's position; unrounded
  layout origins; scroll overflow measured before rounding.
- Lists: estimated heights for unmeasured rows, item remeasurement and
  browser-style scroll anchoring.
- Live views that do not dirty their ancestors; cached views replay their
  last frame; the view cache key includes fade mask, opacity and transform.
- Style transitions and enter animations.
- Paint-time transforms (scale, translate, rotate) applied to primitives,
  masks, hitboxes and accessibility bounds.
- Accessibility: a shared tree served to VoiceOver (macOS) and AT-SPI (Linux)
  through AccessKit (src/accessibility.rs).
- Browser-style keyboard focus: Tab stops, focus-visible rings, tab order
  groups, inert subtrees, focus traps, Enter/Space activation.
- macOS: maximized bounds for zoomed windows, display links that pause when
  idle, an option to keep occluded windows drawing.
- Linux: backdrop passes in the Blade renderer, X11 focus with embedded child
  windows, fontconfig resolution of system and generic font names.
- A backdrop blur example (examples/backdrop_blur.rs).
